  "database": "rschema_0339",
  "question": "\"The API performance management system is used to track and analyze the usage of various APIs across multiple projects. The system is required to record each project's ID, name, and related avatar information. Each project may contain multiple APIs, with each API bound to a project, and the system must record each API's unique identifier, name, and access path. To monitor the performance of the APIs, the system must collect statistics on each API's call frequency, average response time, and 90％ response time. Additionally, the system must record each API's creation and update times to track their development history. Users can view and analyze the performance data of APIs through the system to optimize the response efficiency of the APIs.\"",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0339\n\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `avatar` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `api` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `call_frequency` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `avg_response_time` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `p90_response_time` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `project_id` (`project_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `api_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
